            <div xml:id="d489">

                <pb facs="0715" n="613" sameAs="frus:frus1935v01/pg613"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">765.84/474: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Geneva</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Gilbert</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Geneva</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1935-07-10T16:00:00+01:00">July 10, 1935—4
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received July 10—2:10 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>232. Privately informed that the Secretary General has just received
                    communication from Abyssinian representative at Paris requesting him to
                    communicate to the members of the Council the breakdown of the arbitration
                    procedures at Schweningen [<hi rendition="#italic">Scheveningen</hi>] and
                    requesting that the Council as a matter of urgency consider the situation thus
                    created.</p>
                <p>This is informally interpreted as tantamount to a request for an early
                    extraordinary meeting of the Council. League action, however, has not been
                    determined upon.</p>
                <p>This will probably be given to the press tomorrow.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gilbert</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
